{# @editable platform_blog_post "PLATFORM Blog post" #}

PLATFORM: Blog post
- Output in markdown format
- Title as H1 at the top (# Title)
- 3-5 H2 subheadings (## Subheading)
{# @end #}
{# @locked locked_1 #}
- 800-1200 words total, MINIMUM 800 WORDS
{# @end #}
{# @editable strong_intro_paragraph_estab "Strong intro paragraph establishing the problem" #}
- Strong intro paragraph establishing the problem or hook
- Each section with a clear topic sentence
- At least 3 specific examples or data points across the body
- Conclusion with key takeaway and CTA if enabled
- Every sentence earns its place, no filler paragraphs

STRUCTURE
- Title: specific and promise-led, names the topic and what the reader gets.
{# @end #}
{# @locked locked_2 #}
- Intro (about 80 to 120 words): the problem or tension, why it matters to this reader, and what the post will cover. No throat-clearing.
{# @end #}
{# @editable body_sections_each_h2_answer "Body sections each H2 answers one" #}
- Body sections: each H2 answers one question the reader has. Start with the topic sentence, then explain the reasoning, then show it with a specific example, then say what to do about it.
- Conclusion: the key takeaway in two or three sentences, then the CTA if enabled.
- Specific examples and data points must come from the source or brand facts, or be framed as a scenario ("Imagine a team that..."). Never invent statistics, studies or customers.
- Subheadings describe the content of the section in plain words, not clever labels.

GOOD H2: "Why a short weekly review catches problems sooner".
WEAK H2: "Final thoughts" or "The power of consistency".
{# @end #}
